---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import { evidenceStats, PREPARED } from "@/lib/model";

const e = evidenceStats();
const curated = PREPARED.filter((s) => s.source !== "estimated").length;
const estimated = PREPARED.length - curated;
const figures = [
	[e.total, "grounds tested"],
	[e.checked, "with enough records"],
	[e.good, "match the model"],
] as const;
---

<Base title="About & method" description="How Parava models bird migration and checks it against real sightings.">
	<section class="intro">
		<h1>How Parava works</h1>
		<p class="pitch">A calendar of where each bird should be, checked against where people actually see it.</p>
	</section>

	<div class="column">
		<section>
			<h2>The model</h2>
			<p>
				Every species is split into populations. Each one has a wintering ground, a breeding ground, and a spring and
				autumn route between them. The date sets where each population is: settled, departing, in flight or arriving.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Two kinds of species</h2>
			<p>
				<strong>{curated} species</strong> have flyways mapped by hand.
				<strong>{estimated} more</strong> are migrants of India. Their seasons are estimated from when GBIF records of
				them appear in India each month, adjusted for how much birding happens in that month.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Live sightings</h2>
			<p>
				Recent sightings come from iNaturalist, GBIF and, if you add your own key, eBird. Each one is matched to its
				flyway and compared with where the model expects birds to be, so you can see where the two agree and where they do not.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>How it is checked</h2>
			<ul class="figures">
				{figures.map(([n, label]) => <li><strong>{n}</strong><span>{label}</span></li>)}
			</ul>
			<p>
				For each hand-mapped ground, we count years of GBIF records by month. A ground matches when the months the
				model says birds are there hold clearly more records than chance would give. Re-run with <code>bun run audit</code>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Limits</h2>
			<p>
				This is a model, not tracking data. It shows where a population is typically found, not individual birds, and
				real dates shift with weather and from year to year.
			</p>
		</section>
	</div>
</Base>

<style>
	/* the intro and every section share one left edge, over a soft leaf wash */
	.intro,
	.column { max-width: 760px; margin-inline: auto; }
	.intro { padding: var(--s6) 0 var(--s5); border-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 60% 100% at 50% 0%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 16%, var(--bg)), var(--bg)) fill 0 / / 120px 100vw 0; }
	h1 { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.2rem); }
	.pitch { max-width: 46ch; margin: var(--s3) 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.15rem; }

	/* each section: heading in a narrow left column, its text beside it; split by hairlines, not boxed */
	.column { margin-bottom: var(--s6); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
	.column section { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 200px minmax(0, 1fr); column-gap: var(--s6); row-gap: var(--s4); padding: var(--s5) 0; }
	.column section + section { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
	.column section > * { grid-column: 2; }
	.column section > h2 { grid-column: 1; grid-row: 1 / span 2; }
	h2 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.65; }
	p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.65; }
	p strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
	code { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text); }
	/* three figures split by short rules */
	.figures { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
	.figures li { display: grid; justify-items: start; gap: 2px; }
	.figures li + li { padding-left: var(--s4); border-left: 1px solid var(--line); }
	.figures strong { font-family: var(--font-num); font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.1; font-variant-numeric: lining-nums tabular-nums; }
	.figures span { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; }
	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.column section { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); row-gap: var(--s2); }
		.column section > *,
		.column section > h2 { grid-column: 1; grid-row: auto; }
		.figures { margin: var(--s2) 0; }
	}
	@media (max-width: 560px) {
		.figures strong { font-size: 1.6rem; }
		.figures span { font-size: 0.66rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
	}
</style>
